# AMD64 thunk export spec -- normaliz.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Boltgun imports this module STATICALLY and
# it had no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module
# (c000007b) and the whole image failed to load (c0000135).  Measured: the
# exe's import table names IdnToAscii (ordinal 0).
#
# All 5 exports are declared in winnls.h, which the oracle's default
# translation unit reaches through windows.h, so all 5 are emitted with no
# PROBE-EXTRA.
#
# One thing to watch on this module and no other in this pass: normaliz is
# built EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--data-only, so every entry in its .spec is a
# FORWARD into kernelbase rather than code of its own.  The guest trap
# resolves by name against the native module, which is where a forward is
# resolved anyway -- but that is the first --data-only module to get a thunk,
# so IdnToAscii returning something wrong rather than faulting is the failure
# to look for if this one ever misbehaves.
DLL normaliz.dll
FROM-SPEC auto
